tion is\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨2\\sqrt{t},t⟩,\\,t\\in [1,4].\n$$\n\nThen, the position vectors of the endpoints of the curve are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(1) & =⟨2,1⟩, \\\\ r(4) & =⟨4,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the fundamental theorem for line integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r & =f(r(4))-f(r(1)) \\\\  & =f(4,4)-f(2,1) \\\\  & =({4}^{2}+{e}^{4\\cdot 4})-({2}^{2}+{e}^{2\\cdot 1}) \\\\  & =(16+{e}^{16})-(4+{e}^{2}) \\\\  & ={e}^{16}-{e}^{2}+12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324856 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324856 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324856 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "69c13dff-cd6b-59c8-8afc-6e8f8eabf8f5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325032 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{ln}^{2}⁡2)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325032 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325032 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7e0e1662-5531-5797-9a2d-180d1aefa39b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325474 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325474 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325474 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b060de89-9a07-5c08-8a5a-902923743941" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325922 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325922 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325922 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "df7d018d-9bcc-56b5-9a57-3f93a49339b0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326186 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+{ln}^{2}⁡2)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326186 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326186 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fba1ed0a-e6ae-5b81-9e9c-40ba51cc6012" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326529 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186324856 #edb/ref 1759